# Net-ISP-Balance on Gentoo Linux

Net-ISP-Balance has been adapted to run natively on Gentoo Linux, respecting Portage sandboxing and OpenRC service management.

## Configuration
The default configuration directory for Gentoo is `/etc/net-isp-balance`.
You should define your ISP interfaces in `/etc/net-isp-balance/balance.conf`.

## Service Management (OpenRC)
An OpenRC service script is provided. To start the load balancer and link status monitor daemon:
```bash
rc-service net-isp-balance start
```

To enable it at boot:
```bash
rc-update add net-isp-balance default
```

## Network Lifecycle Hooks (netifrc)
For maximum reliability, you should trigger routing updates when your network interfaces physical states change. Instead of Debian's `/etc/network/if-up.d/`, Gentoo uses `/etc/conf.d/net` hooks.

You can add the following to your `/etc/conf.d/net` to automatically notify the load balancer:

```bash
postup() {
    # Notify Net-ISP-Balance that an interface came up
    if rc-service net-isp-balance status | grep -q "started"; then
        /usr/bin/load_balance.pl
    fi
    return 0
}

postdown() {
    # Notify Net-ISP-Balance that an interface went down
    if rc-service net-isp-balance status | grep -q "started"; then
        /usr/bin/load_balance.pl
    fi
    return 0
}
```
